  "summary": "Malicious code in bnpl-blocks-atom-bnpl-dolyame-button (npm)",
  "details": "A fake UI-component package (index.js is a stub class) that, on require, runs setup.js: it fingerprints the platform/arch, then downloads a second-stage binary from Cloudflare Workers endpoints (oob-worker[.]cf100-416[.]workers[.]dev, oob-worker[.]cf101-adf[.]workers[.]dev, oob-worker[.]cf102-baf[.]workers[.]dev, oob-worker[.]cf103-070[.]workers[.]dev) at paths /pkg/package, /pkg/package-arm64, /pkg/loader_mac, or /pkg/package.exe. If the HTTPS download fails it falls back to reconstructing the payload from DNS TXT records served by c[.]sdk[.]dl[.]wel1[.]ru (and ext/pkg/net[.]dl[.]wel1[.]ru per-platform). The downloaded binary is written to a temp file (.cache_\u003chex\u003e on Unix, dotnet_diag_\u003chex\u003e.exe on Windows) and executed detached via /bin/sh or cmd.exe /c start /b, so it outlives the parent process. The payload is fetched from attacker-controlled infrastructure and executed on the installer's machine.",
  "affected": [
